   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello Phil,<br><br>I want to fit a multidimensional GPCM to my data (2000 observations of 31 Likert-type items with 5 categories) in order to develop a multidimensional CAT.<br><br>First, I fitted the model to my data using this the following syntax:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">mm </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mirt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;gpcm&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> method </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;MHRM&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  technical </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">MAXQUAD </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">20000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NCYCLES </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>Then, I estimated factor scores using MAP estimation (which is recommended to use when dealing with high numbers of latent traits) with the following syntax:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">scores </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fscores</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> method </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;MAP&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> full</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">scores </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>In order to get complete response patterns for my incomplete observations (needed to perform CAT simulations), I fitted again the same model with imputed data:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">mm2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mirt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">imputeMissing</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">scores</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;gpcm&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> method </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;MHRM&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> technical </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">MAXQUAD </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">20000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NCYCLES </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>Finally, I printed the results of the two models:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mm<br><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Call</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>mirt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> dat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> itemtype </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;gpcm&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> method </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;MHRM&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>    technical </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">MAXQUAD </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">20000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NCYCLES </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Full</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">information item factor analysis </span><span style=\"color:#008\">with</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">9</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> factor</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">s</span><span style=\"color:#660\">).</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Converged</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> within </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.001</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> tolerance after </span><span style=\"color:#066\">940</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> MHRM iterations</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>mirt version</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>M</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">step optimizer</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NR <br><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">likelihood </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">73479.22</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> SE </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.104</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>AIC </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">147334.4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">AICc</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">147373.8</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>BIC </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">148386.7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> SABIC </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">147789.4</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mm2<br><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Call</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>mirt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> imputeMissing</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> scores</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> itemtype </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;gpcm&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>    method </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;MHRM&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> technical </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">MAXQUAD </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">20000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NCYCLES </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Full</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">information item factor analysis </span><span style=\"color:#008\">with</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">9</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> factor</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">s</span><span style=\"color:#660\">).</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Converged</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> within </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.001</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> tolerance after </span><span style=\"color:#066\">915</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> MHRM iterations</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>mirt version</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>M</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">step optimizer</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NR <br><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">likelihood </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">77555.71</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> SE </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.096</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>AIC </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">155487.4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">AICc</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">155526.8</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>BIC </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">156539.6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> SABIC </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">155942.3</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>Given the information criteria (AIC and BIC), it seems that the first model (with incomplete data) is better than the second (with imputed data).<br><br>I would expect the opposite result, have you got an idea on this ?<br><br>Thank you.<br><br>Pierre<br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "udxqv2ohBD4J",
   "from": "Phil Chalmers",
