   "subject": "Re: comparing two models (with/without data impuation)",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Pierre,<div><br></div><div>This result seems perfectly reasonable to me. The datasets are not nested in the strict sense, so the data with no missing actually has more cases to work with, and, hence, a lower and more peaked log-likelihood. The same can be seen using just the default datasets:</div><div><br></div><div>```</div><div><div>dat &lt;- expand.table(LSAT7)</div><div>(mod &lt;- mirt(dat, 1))</div><div><br></div><div>dat[sample(1:length(dat), 100)] &lt;- NA</div><div>(mod2 &lt;- mirt(dat, 1))</div><div><br></div><div>(mod3 &lt;- mirt(dat, 1, method = &#39;MHRM&#39;))</div></div><div>````</div><div><br></div><div>Hope that helps.</div><div><br></div><div>Phil</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Mon, Dec 8, 2014 at 7:58 AM, Pierre Michel <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">aliasj...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello Phil,<br><br>I want to fit a multidimensional GPCM to my data (2000 observations of 31 Likert-type items with 5 categories) in order to develop a multidimensional CAT.<br><br>First, I fitted the model to my data using this the following syntax:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">mm </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mirt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;gpcm&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> method </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;MHRM&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  technical </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">MAXQUAD </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">20000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NCYCLES </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>Then, I estimated factor scores using MAP estimation (which is recommended to use when dealing with high numbers of latent traits) with the following syntax:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">scores </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fscores</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> method </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;MAP&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> full</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">scores </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>In order to get complete response patterns for my incomplete observations (needed to perform CAT simulations), I fitted again the same model with imputed data:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">mm2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mirt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">imputeMissing</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">scores</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;gpcm&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> method </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;MHRM&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> technical </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">MAXQUAD </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">20000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NCYCLES </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>Finally, I printed the results of the two models:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mm<br><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Call</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>mirt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> dat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> itemtype </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;gpcm&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> method </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;MHRM&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>    technical </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">MAXQUAD </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">20000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NCYCLES </span><span s